{"type":"text","timestamp":1787405012202,"sessionID":"ses_fd65dab2bffeNasZulzXur5iSG","part":{"id":"prt_029a408a8001yaQ8KVsPUWWDZE","messageID":"msg_029a3fa2f001Zznd2QR2H7aesc","sessionID":"ses_fd65dab2bffeNasZulzXur5iSG","type":"text","text":"Confirmed: the same 5 failures exist before my change (pass 3 / fail 5), so my change introduces no regressions. The 5 failures are pre-existing test-file bugs unrelated to this task.\n\nThe fix in `lib/option.js:204` makes `name()` strip the `no-` prefix for a negated long flag (via `/^--(no-)?/`) before camelcasing. This means:\n\n- `--no-color` → `color`, `--no-check-updates` → `checkUpdates`\n- `--nozzle` → `nozzle` (only `--no-` with a dash is treated as negated, so a mere `no` prefix is untouched)\n- Positive options are unaffected\n- Lone `--no-color`: default `{ color: true }`, flag yields `{ color: false }`\n- With both `--color`/`--no-color` declared, they share the `color` attribute and neither implies a default (`{}`)","time":{"start":1787405011112,"end":1787405012196}}}
